From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Burr <chrisburr73@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 01:57:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Initialise the zsh completion harness locals explicitly

`typeset NAME` in zsh prints `NAME=value` when the parameter already
exists, so when PREFIX is exported in the environment the harness writes
an extra line to stdout and the captured completion output no longer
matches. It also means the harness starts with the inherited value of
PREFIX rather than an empty one.

Conda build and test environments always export PREFIX, which makes
test_zsh_completion_lists_dsn_aliases_in_supported_contexts fail there
whenever zsh is installed.

Give the three parameters explicit empty initialisers, which both
suppresses the printing and gives the harness the empty starting state it
assumes.
---
 test/pytests/test_zsh_completion.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/pytests/test_zsh_completion.py b/test/pytests/test_zsh_completion.py
index 3a6f3d6..b5a87d7 100644
--- a/test/pytests/test_zsh_completion.py
+++ b/test/pytests/test_zsh_completion.py
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@ _path_files() {
 }
 
 typeset -a captured compset_calls path_file_calls
-typeset PREFIX IPREFIX used_unambiguous
+typeset PREFIX='' IPREFIX='' used_unambiguous=''
 compadd() {
     local array_name=''
     local candidate
